Correct Way to Create Comment Snippets in VS Code
Open VS Code Snippet Configuration:

Press Ctrl+Shift+P (Windows/Linux) or Cmd+Shift+P (Mac)

Type "Preferences: Configure User Snippets"

Select "New Global Snippets File"

Name it terraform.json (this creates a new snippets file specifically for Terraform)

Add This Code (replace the entire file contents):

json
{
  "Big Section Header": {
    "prefix": "bigheader",
    "body": [
      "##########################################",
      "### ${1:SECTION_NAME}",
      "##########################################",
      "$0"
    ],
    "description": "Large formatted section header"
  },
  "Box Comment": {
    "prefix": "boxcomment",
    "body": [
      "/*",
      " * ${1:COMMENT_TEXT}",
      " */",
      "$0"
    ],
    "description": "Box-style block comment"
  }
}
Usage:

In any .tf file, type bigheader then press Tab for a large comment block